iness from Rede D’Or, the largest integrated health care network in Brazil, and from private equity fund Opus Investimentos, which have supported the development of GSH for more than eight years.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:fca0b20bc2f0def4e913a3d65831d855","date":"2025-04-23","date_text":null,"kind":"debt_financing","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"American Heart of Poland","portco_name":null,"target_website":null,"investor":"CVC Credit","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"CVC Credit provides debt facilities to American Heart of Poland through its Capital Solutions strategy","summary":"CVC Credit provided debt facilities to Gruppo San Donato-owned American Heart of Poland to finance its acquisition of Scanmed.","source_name":"CVC Capital Partners","source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2025/cvc-credit-provides-debt-facilities-to-american-heart-of-poland-through-its-capital-solutions-strategy/","evidence":"CVC Credit is pleased to announce that it has provided debt facilities to American Heart of Poland (“AHP”), the top-ranked privately operated cardiology focused public healthcare services provider in Poland, owned by Gruppo San Donato, the leading private and public hospital group in Italy.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:bdc64baf8ddcbd3f51c6dd13bd2c18e8","date":"2025-04-29","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Omada","portco_name":"Omada","target_website":null,"investor":"GRO Fund III","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":["Kirk Kapital"],"seller":"CVC Growth Funds and GRO Fund II","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"CVC Growth Funds announce exit of Omada","summary":"GRO Fund III and Kirk Kapital agreed to acquire identity governance software firm Omada, a full exit for CVC Growth Funds and GRO Fund II.","source_name":"CVC Capital Partners","source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2025/cvc-growth-funds-announce-exit-of-omada/","evidence":"Omada A/S (“Omada”), a global leader in Identity Governance and Administration (IGA) software, today announced that GRO Fund III, the latest fund managed by GRO, together with Kirk Kapital has agreed to acquire the company from its existing shareholders.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:02163fe4e706e89080c4a91f590f6b7d","date":"2025-05-01","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Dream Games","portco_name":"Dream Games","target_website":"dreamgames.com","investor":"CVC","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Blackstone"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Dream Games announces strategic investment by CVC to support next chapter of growth and continued global leadership in mobile games","summary":"CVC made a strategic investment in mobile games developer Dream Games as sole equity partner, buying out its early venture investors, with Blackstone funds and others providing debt.","source_name":"CVC Capital Partners","source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2025/dream-games-announces-strategic-investment-by-cvc-to-support-next-chapter-of-growth-and-continued-global-leadership-in-mobile-games/","evidence":"Dream Games, the developer and publisher of globally renowned mobile games Royal Match and Royal Kingdom, today announced a strategic investment from CVC, a leading global alternative asset management firm, as its sole equity partner.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:1fe66daaefd44a2d839b7d6f54628098","date":"2025-05-20","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Genetic","portco_name":"Genetic Group","targe