/2014/2014-02-05-cvc-fund-v-invests-in-avast-to-drive-us-and-mobile-growth/","evidence":"The investment, which values AVAST at $1 billion, will position the company to expand its global reach into mobile security and the USA.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:2fc368c383746a46412b9259d47f7985","date":"2014-03-17","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Da Niang Dumpling","portco_name":"Da Niang Dumpling","target_website":null,"investor":"CVC Asia III","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Mr. Wu Guoqiang","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"CVC Asia III completes acquisition of stake in Da Niang Dumpling","summary":"CVC-advised funds completed the acquisition of a controlling stake in Chinese QSR operator Da Niang Dumpling from its founder.","source_name":"CVC Capital Partners","source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2014/2014-03-17-cvc-asia-iii-completes-acquisition-of-stake-in-da-niang-dumpling/","evidence":"Funds advised by CVC Capital Partners (\"CVC\") today announced the completion of the acquisition of a controlling stake in Da Niang Dumpling Holdings Limited (\"Da Niang\"), a leading Chinese cuisine quick-service restaurant operator in China, from the founder Mr. Wu Guoqiang, who will remain as a shareholder.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:7c9c6e29671d04bf6918a45e69d5b197","date":"2014-03-25","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Synsam","portco_name":"Synsam","target_website":"synsam.se","investor":"CVC Fund V","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":"Alipes AB and former store owners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"CVC Fund V agrees to acquire Synsam Nordic from Alipes","summary":"CVC-advised funds acquired Nordic optical retailer Synsam from Alipes and former store owners.","source_name":"CVC Capital Partners","source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2014/2014-03-25-cvc-fund-v-agrees-to-acquire-synsam-nordic-from-alipes/","evidence":"Funds advised by CVC Capital Partners (\"CVC\") today announced the successful acquisition of Synsam Nordic A/S (\"Synsam\"), the leading optical retailer in the Nordic region, from Alipes AB (\"Alipes\") and former store owners.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:56b517a3db54b84c019b07435e97dade","date":"2014-04-10","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Flint Group","portco_name":"Flint Group","target_website":null,"investor":"Goldman Sachs Merchant Banking Division","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":["Koch Equity Development"],"seller":"CVC Capital Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":100.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Goldman Sachs and Koch Industries to acquire Flint Group from CVC Funds","summary":"Goldman Sachs Merchant Banking and Koch Equity Development agreed to acquire 100% of printing inks supplier Flint Group from CVC-advised funds.","source_name":"CVC Capital Partners","source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2014/2014-04-10-goldman-sachs-and-koch-industries-to-acquire-flint-group-from-cvc-funds/","evidence":"Goldman Sachs Merchant Banking Division announced today that it has partnered with Koch Equity Development LLC, a subsidiary of Koch Industries, Inc., to acquire shares representing 100% of Flint Group's share capital from funds advised by private equity firm CVC Capital Partners.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:37df698946aace329d7a31507e9ac57b","date":"2014-04-25","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"South Beauty","portco_name":"South Beauty","target_website":null,"investor":"CVC Asia III","sponsor_is_